{# "N senders are waiting for your review" — the quantified call to action.

   Rendered on BOTH the domain detail page and the Sender Inventory page so the
   expected action is stated wherever the amber badges appear, not only once
   the per-row advisor thresholds are crossed. Renders nothing when there is
   nothing to decide.

   `needsDecisionCount` is the higher-confidence subset — senders with enough
   30-day history for the SenderAuthorizationAdvisor to actually recommend a
   verdict. It is offered as a shortcut ("start with these"), never as a
   replacement for the honest total.

   Props:
     - domainId           (string)   domain to link the filtered list for
     - needsReviewCount   (int)      senders in the Needs review state
     - needsReviewMessages(int)      lifetime volume those senders carry (materiality)
     - needsDecisionCount (int)      subset the advisor has a recommendation for
#}
{% props domainId, needsReviewCount = 0, needsReviewMessages = 0, needsDecisionCount = 0 %}

{% if needsReviewCount > 0 %}
    <div class="card border border-warning/30 bg-warning/5 shadow-sm mb-6"
         data-testid="sender-review-cta">
        <div class="card-body p-4 sm:p-5">
            <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <div class="w-9 h-9 rounded-full bg-warning/15 text-warning flex items-center justify-center shrink-0">
                    <svg class="w-5 h-5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                        <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4m6 2a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z"/>
                    </svg>
                </div>

                <div class="flex-1 min-w-0">
                    <h3 class="font-semibold text-sm sm:text-base" data-testid="sender-review-cta-headline">
                        {{ needsReviewCount }} sender{{ needsReviewCount == 1 ? '' : 's' }} waiting for your review
                    </h3>

                    <p class="text-sm text-base-content/70 mt-1 leading-relaxed max-w-3xl">
                        {% if needsReviewMessages > 0 %}
                            They have sent {{ needsReviewMessages|number_format(0, '.', ',') }} message{{ needsReviewMessages == 1 ? '' : 's' }} as this domain
                            and carry a <span class="badge badge-xs badge-warning align-middle">Needs review</span> badge because nobody has said yet whether they are yours.
                        {% else %}
                            Each carries a <span class="badge badge-xs badge-warning align-middle">Needs review</span> badge because nobody has said yet whether it is yours.
                        {% endif %}
                        Marking them costs nothing and changes no DNS — it just stops Sendvery flagging mail you already trust.
                    </p>

                    <p class="text-xs text-base-content/60 mt-2 max-w-3xl">
                        <strong class="text-base-content/80">If you do nothing:</strong> no mail is blocked or released, but these
                        senders keep showing up amber here, in your alerts and in your weekly email.
                    </p>

                    <div class="mt-3 flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center gap-2 sm:gap-3 flex-wrap">
                        <a href="{{ path('dashboard_sender_inventory', { domainId: domainId, filter: 'needs_review' }) }}"
                           class="btn btn-sm btn-warning"
                           data-testid="sender-review-cta-primary">
                            Review {{ needsReviewCount }} sender{{ needsReviewCount == 1 ? '' : 's' }}
                        </a>

                        {% if needsDecisionCount > 0 %}
                            <a href="{{ path('dashboard_sender_inventory', { domainId: domainId, recommendation: 'needs_decision' }) }}"
                               class="btn btn-sm btn-ghost"
                               data-testid="sender-needs-decision-stat">
                                Start with the {{ needsDecisionCount }} we can advise on
                            </a>
                        {% endif %}

                        <a href="{{ path('knowledge_base_article', { slug: 'authorizing-senders-explained' }) }}"
                           class="link link-hover text-xs sm:text-sm text-base-content/70"
                           data-testid="sender-review-cta-kb-link">
                            How do I tell if a sender is really mine? →
                        </a>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
{% endif %}
